title: "Odd-Color Amplitude Filters for Lonely Runner Riesz Products"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dehmiwal"
    given-names: "Jatin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Legedith/lonely-runner"
url: "https://legedith.github.io/lonely-runner/"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
keywords:
  - "Lonely Runner Conjecture"
  - "Riesz products"
  - "odd coloring"
  - "hypergraph coloring"
  - "correlated amplitudes"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formal verification"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked finite cancellation interface for Riesz-product approaches
  to the Lonely Runner Conjecture. On every even relation support, an explicit
  positive-mean correlated two-color law has zero mixed moment if and only if
  the support is odd-colored. Independent sharp scalar filters handle odd
  support sizes, and failure of odd two-colorability yields a parity-circuit
  obstruction over F_2.
